From 135bd1d0b61bbf199b175610c3bc03ab6d796e2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:43:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] protected-wins: kv-zero-freed-cells is default ON in v0.1.3.1
 (6b709b4507), id drops -opt-in

HQ84 item 3 ruled kv-zero ships default ON. The entry registered at 54af6cdd89 described it as opt-in, default OFF; it now names the flip commit, the =0 merge-base switch and the measured cost (not a speed win).

Origin: lane-298
Measured-effect: none (registry text; receipts are lane 300 cell 31: c31p-10070726, c31q-10070739, c31o-10070746, c31o-10070901)
---
 tools/arifi-sync/protected-wins.json | 16 +++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/arifi-sync/protected-wins.json b/tools/arifi-sync/protected-wins.json
index 191ddcf6cb..5d1f1e770b 100644
--- a/tools/arifi-sync/protected-wins.json
+++ b/tools/arifi-sync/protected-wins.json
@@ -2283,14 +2283,15 @@
       "_registered": "2026-10-06, lane 298 relaunch-62 (HQ82 Q41 answer (a))."
     },
     {
-      "id": "kv-zero-freed-cells-opt-in",
+      "id": "kv-zero-freed-cells",
       "status": "active",
-      "_registered": "2026-10-07, lane 298 relaunch-78 (point release v0.1.3.1 integration owner), from lane 300's commit trailers and MERGE-READY (cache/determinism-x1-lane/MERGE-READY.md, branch lane-300/kv-zero). OPT-IN, default OFF: protected so the switch and its zeroing path survive merges, not as a speed win.",
-      "mechanism": "F-141 producer fix: KV cells freed by seq_rm / a rewind are zeroed before any later read, inside the mid-decode window bound [n_kv_prev, n_kv), with a transposed-V block assert and one INFO line naming the zeroing. LLAMA_ARIFI_KV_ZERO_FREED=1 turns it on; unset or 0 = the merge-base path (the third commit moved the default 1 -> 0 after cell 31's pooled-cost clause failed).",
